          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Recall that the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+object"} support object
            of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncation"} (-1)-truncation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to 1
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert X \Vert
            denote its support.
          %p
            We say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has a
            %strong split support
            if the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/map"} map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to {\Vert X \Vert}
            has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert X \Vert
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+object"} subterminal object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert X \Vert} \to X
          %p
            If all objects has split supports, we say that
            %strong supports split
            in the ambient category.
          %h2#relation_to_axiom_of_choice Relation to axiom of choice
          %p
            Supports splitting in a category is a weak form of the external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            (all regular epis split). In fact, the splitting of supports is exactly the “difference” between the external axiom of choice and the
            %em internal
            axiom of choice, i.e.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi EAC
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi IAC
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext and
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EAC \Leftrightarrow (IAC \;\text{ and }\; SS).
          %h2#in_foundations In foundations
          %h3#in_set_theory In set theory
          %p
            If we assume
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointedness
            %em function
            assigning to every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a section of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to {\Vert X \Vert}
            is much stronger: such a function is a global
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/choice+operator"} choice operator
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            %a{:href => "#FourmanScedrov"} (Fourman-Scedrov)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KECA"} (KECA)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
          %h3#in_homotopy_type_theory In (homotopy) type theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            under
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            %em function
            as above called the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/choice+operator"} choice operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a section of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to {\Vert X \Vert}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+axiom+of+choice"} global axiom of choice
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi Type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{(X:Type)} \Vert ( \Vert X \Vert \to X ) \Vert.
          %p
            We might pronounce this version as “all supports
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} merely
            split”.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mi Type
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{(X:Type)} \Vert X \Vert \to X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
          %h4#objects_with_split_support Objects with split support
          %p
            Since not all supports split in homotopy type theory, it is interesting to consider whether the support of some particular type is split. For instance, for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi qinv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} qinv(f) \coloneqq \sum_{g:B\to A} (f g = id_B) \times (g f = id_A)
            has split support, since its support can be proven to be equal to the type of coherent equivalence data on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            It is shown in
            %a{:href => "#KECA"} (KECA)
            that a type in homotopy type theory has split support if and only if it admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/steady+function"} steady
            endomap. Thus, it has merely split support if and only if it merely admits a steady endomap.
          %p
            Some general classes of types can be shown
            %em not
            to have split support, at least not uniformly, by arguments similar to the one which shows that not all types have split support. For instance, the identity type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=_A y
            has split support for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y:A
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KECA"} (KECA)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+HoTT+book"} the HoTT book
          %p Similarly, we have:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If the type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi steady
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} steady(f)\coloneqq \prod_{(x,y:A+A)} (f x = f y)
              has split support for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomap"} endomap
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A+A\to A+A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b:A
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert a=b\Vert
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a=b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a set. Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g,h : A \to A+A
              to be constant at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inl(a)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inl(b)
              respectively, and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = [g,h] : A+A \to A+A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi steady
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} steady(f) =  ( (A\times A) \to ((a=a) \times (a=b) \times (b=a) \times (b=b)) )
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert a=b\Vert
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi steady
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert steady(f)\Vert
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi steady
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} steady(f)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a=b
          %p
            In particular, not all types of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi steady
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} steady(f)
            have split support. Thus, “steadiness” is not as well-behaved a notion as being quasi-invertible.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#FourmanScedrov
              %p
                M. P. Fourman and A. Scedrov. The “world’s simplest axiom of choice” fails.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Manuscripta Math.
            %li#KECA
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Kraus"}> Nicolai Kraus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Escardo"} Martin Escardo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"} Thierry Coquand
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thorsten+Altenkirch"} Thorsten Altenkirch
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalizations of Hedberg’s theorem
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/papers/hedberg.pdf"} PDF
              %p (In this paper, types with split support are called “h-stable”)
